# This project deploys to a Linux device (Raspberry Pi) even when developed on
# Windows. Force LF line endings for anything that gets executed as a shell
# script, read by systemd/udev, or fed line-by-line to a Linux tool (apt,
# xargs, ...) on the Pi, regardless of the checking-out platform's
# core.autocrlf setting. This isn't just cosmetic: a CRLF shell script fails
# outright on Linux ("$'\r': command not found"), and a CRLF requirements
# file makes every single package "unlocatable" - xargs/apt treat the
# trailing \r as part of the package name. pip tolerates CRLF in
# requirements.txt so that half of install/ never showed symptoms, which is
# what made this easy to only half-fix the first time around.
*.sh text eol=lf
.envrc text eol=lf
install/** text eol=lf
scripts/pidisplay_netmon/** text eol=lf
